# Swipe Cards — Tinder-style stack of 9 photo cards with like/dislike/reset buttons.
# What this test covers: a short drag released under the translation+velocity
# threshold springs back; slow drags past width/3 swipe right and left; a fast
# fling past the threshold; the heart and X buttons swipe the top card; rapid
# repeated button taps run the stack to the end (pressing past the last card
# must be a no-op); reset springs every card back with staggered timeouts and
# is interrupted by a new swipe mid-flight; reset tapped twice in a row.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/swipe-cards"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
wait 1500
# Drag under the threshold, release: card springs back.
gesture pan 200 380 60 0 600
wait 800
# Slow drags past the threshold in both directions.
gesture pan 200 380 180 20 400
wait 1000
gesture pan 200 380 -180 -20 400
wait 1000
# Quick flick.
gesture fling left 200 380 150
wait 1000
gesture fling right 200 380 150
wait 1000
# Buttons: heart (like), X (dislike) — unlabeled, tap by position.
press 301 777
wait 700
press 101 777
wait 700
# Rapid taps run the stack out; extra taps past the last card do nothing.
press 301 777 --count 6
wait 1500
press 101 777
wait 500
# Reset all cards, interrupt the staggered reset with a swipe.
press 201 777
wait 300
gesture pan 200 380 180 0 300
wait 1500
press 201 777
wait 100
press 201 777
wait 2000
# Stack is back: swipe the top card again.
gesture pan 200 380 -180 0 400
wait 1000
press 201 777
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 3000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\" id=\"xmark\""
wait 1500
